---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import StatusBadge from "../components/StatusBadge.astro";
import { features, verifiedOn, toolchainVersion, toolchainArchive, toolchainSha256 } from "../data/features";
---

<Base title="Transparency" description="The exact verified feature matrix for the RUDRA v1.1.0 toolchain, with evidence and honest limitations." path="/transparency">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:860px">
      <p class="eyebrow">Transparency</p>
      <h1>Verification matrix and evidence</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The statuses below come from independent testing of the shipped
        toolchain. No capability is listed as working unless it was compiled
        and run. No benchmarks, download counts or community statistics are
        published anywhere on this site.
      </p>

      <div class="callout callout-info" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <h4>What was tested</h4>
        <p>
          Archive <code>{toolchainArchive}</code> (RUDRA {toolchainVersion}),
          SHA256 <code style="word-break:break-all">{toolchainSha256}</code>,
          verified on {verifiedOn}. The checksum was confirmed before
          extraction. Tests ran on Linux x86_64.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top:2.2rem">Feature matrix</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>Status</th><th>API</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {features.map((f) => (
            <tr>
              <td><strong>{f.name}</strong></td>
              <td><StatusBadge status={f.status} /></td>
              <td>{f.api ? <code>{f.api}</code> : <span style="color:var(--text-faint)">n/a</span>}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 style="margin-top:2.2rem">Evidence</h2>
      {features.map((f) => (
        <div class="card" style="margin-top:0.9rem">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:1.05rem">{f.name}</h3>
            <StatusBadge status={f.status} />
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:0.92rem;margin:0.6rem 0 0">{f.evidence}</p>
        </div>
      ))}

      <h2 style="margin-top:2.5rem">Known discrepancies and limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The distributed binaries are <strong>dynamically linked</strong>. Distribution text describing the toolchain as having zero external dependencies or requiring no linker is not supported by the shipped binaries and is corrected here.</li>
        <li>The documented channel functions <code>send</code> and <code>recv</code> do not exist in the shipped binary. The working functions are <code>chan_send</code> and <code>chan_recv</code>.</li>
        <li>A function named <code>json_parse</code> does not exist in the shipped binary. JSON object reading works via <code>json_get</code>.</li>
        <li><code>http_get</code> opens a real TCP connection but does not resolve hostnames (no DNS) and does not implement HTTPS or TLS.</li>
        <li>Mutex ran in a single-threaded program; cross-thread contention correctness was not independently proven.</li>
        <li>No guarantee is made that the software is free of defects or vulnerabilities.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:2rem">Status definitions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>VERIFIED</strong> - compiled and run with the expected result.</li>
        <li><strong>PARTIALLY VERIFIED</strong> - present and runs, but a part of the claim was not fully exercised.</li>
        <li><strong>PLANNED</strong> - documented as roadmap, not shipped.</li>
        <li><strong>NOT VERIFIED</strong> - could not be confirmed, or observed not to work as documented.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
